Name xml:lang="bo">རིན་ཆེན་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rat+na kir+ti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ratna kirti</persName><birth notBefore="1100-01-01">after 1100</birth><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8LS15361</idno><idno type="APIS">4674</idno><note type="comment">His name in Tibetan can be reconstructed as "Rin chen grags."&#13;
He composed work (ID:5131) in his 80th year.</note></person><person xml:id="person7024"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bstan 'dzin</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">བསྟན་འཛིན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos smra ba'i gshes bsnyen shes ldan gzu bor gnas pa'i don gnyer ba bstan 'dzin</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos smra ba'i bshes gsnyen shes ldan gzu bor gnas pa'i don gnyer ba bstan 'dzin</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">7024</idno><note type="comment">Reading of the name uncertain.</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work5131"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mtha' bral dbu ma'i rnam bzhag gsal byed sgron me</title><title xml:lang="bo">མཐའ་བྲལ་དབུ་མའི་རྣམ་བཞག་གསལ་བྱེད་སྒྲོན་མེ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mtha' bral dbu ma chen po'i gnas lugs gsal bar byed pa'i gsal byed sgron me</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ratna kir tis mdzad pa'i mtha' bral dbu ma'i rnam gzhag gsal byed sgron me</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1127-01-01">after 1127</date><author ref="person:4674">rin chen grags</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The work was composed in the year "me mo lugs gi lo smin drug zla ba'i dkar phyogs" - {Kārttika śukla pakṣa} = 1127, 1187, 1247, 1307, 1367... - when the author (ID:4674) was 80 years old.&#13;
&#13;
The work is generally practice/meditation orientated and discusses the correct understanding of Mahāmudrā. Also mentioned are the arising of the "thal 'gyur pa"  in Tibet following Pa tshab (ID:3868)'s return (before which, according to the author, only the "rang rgyud pa" was attested in Tibet), and the ulterior emergence of the rang stong/gzhan stong distinction ((ID:5130), fol. 18.1b4-5).&#13;
&#13;
The author mentions a "zla 'od gzhon nu" who might be sGam po pa ex64082024-12-1910-05-06 .</note><respStmt><resp>prompter</resp><name ref="person:7024">bstan 'dzin</name></respStmt><idno type="APIS">5131</idno></bibl></listBibl><listPlace><place xml:id="place5558"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rgya gar</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">རྒྱ་གར</placeName><idno type="APIS">5558</idno></place><place xml:id="place5559"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bod</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">བོད</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">gangs ri'i khrod la kha ba can gyi ljongs</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">ri bo gangs can</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">gangs ri'i khrod</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">gangs can</placeName><idno type="APIS">5559</idno></place><place xml:id="place5699"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dpal glang ri thang</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">དཔལ་གླང་རི་ཐང</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">dpal glang ri thang gi gtsug lag khang</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">glang thang</placeName><idno type="APIS">5699</idno></place></listPlace><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel4725" name="requests" active="#person7024" passive="#person4674" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex64082023-09-261"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel4728" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person4674" passive="#person3868" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel935" name="author-of" active="#person4674" passive="#work5131" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex64082023-09-261"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel4727" name="quotes-with-name" active="#person4674" passive="#person4189" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex64082024-12-1910-05-06"/></desc></relation><relation xml:id="rel4726" name="active-at" active="#person4674" passive="#place5699" type="positive"><desc>Evidence: <ptr target="#ex64082023-09-261"/></desc></relation><relation 